<title>USA: Texaco names Judge Higginbotham an advisor.</title>
<headline>Texaco names Judge Higginbotham an advisor.</headline>
<dateline>WHITE PLAINS, N.Y. 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Texaco Inc said on Tuesday that it made a formal agreement with Judge A. Leon Higginbotham Jr to serve as an advisor to provide counsel and guidance as the company reviews its human resource and diversity policies and practices.</p>
<p>Peter Bijur, Texaco's chairman and chief executive, said Higginbotham will evaluate company policies and make recommendations for change.</p>
<p>&quot;I want to ensure that Texaco's policies prohibiting discrimination in the workplace are not mere rhetoric,&quot; Bijur said in a company release.</p>
</text>
